cc6a63c9-7482-5e58-94cf-dffcb3862ae0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395066 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186395067 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395066 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95724" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395066 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395066 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that\n\n$\\,$ ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\n\nare eigenvectors of a $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix $A$ that correspond to the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=3$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=1,$ respectively. Find the matrix $A.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395066 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4f741f54-e9ba-55b4-9c81-df73745d51c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186395066 #edb/ref 1074 "The spectral decomposition of a $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\lambda }_{1}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1}^{T}+{\\lambda }_{2}{u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere ${u}_{1}$ and ${u}_{2}$ are orthonormal eigenvectors of $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2},$ respectively.\n\nFirst, let's normalize our eigenvectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}_{2} & =\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\lambda }_{1}{u}_{1}{u}_{1}^{T}+{\\lambda }_{2}{u}_{2}{u}_{2}^{T} \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1\\end{aligned}]+1\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1\\end{aligned}]+1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1\\end{align